Footnotes:
"1. Data are not available for this area for all of the requested years. See Caveats below for more information."
"2. No data are available for individual Alaskan areas prior to 1989. In 1994, data for 5 Alaskan areas (Aleutians East,"
"Aleutians West, Lake and Peninsula, Skagway-Hoonah-Angoon, Yakutat) become available and data for 2 Alaskan areas (Aleutians"
"Islands and Skagway-Yakutat-Angoon) are no longer available. During 1989-98, some Alaskan areas experience boundary changes. See"
"Caveats below for more information."
"---"
Caveats:
"1. For CMF 1979-1998, county-level data are not available for individual Alaskan areas before data year 1989. Location code"
"02900 represents all Alaskan areas before 1989. More information: http://wonder.cdc.gov/wonder/help/cmf.html#02900."
"2. For CMF 1979-1998, data for the Aleutian Islands Census Area, Alaska (FIPS code 02010) are available only for 1989-1993."
"Beginning with data year 1994, deaths and population counts for this area are divided between Aleutians East Borough (FIPS code"
"02013) and Aleutians West Census Area (FIPS code 02016)."
"3. For CMF 1979-1998, data for the following counties are available beginning in data year data 1994, and thus the 1994"
"population estimates are referenced for cell suppression purposes instead of the 1990 population estimates: Aleutians East"
"Borough (02013), Aleutians West Census Area (02016), Lake and Peninsula Borough (02164), Skagway-Hoonah-Angoon Census Area"
"(02232), Yakutat Borough (02282) Alaska and La Paz (04012), Arizona."
"4. Data for Denali Borough (FIPS code 02068) are not available on the CMF 1979-98. Deaths and population counts for Denali"
"Borough are aggregated with those for Yukon-Koyukuk (FIPS code 02290)."
"5. For CMF 1979-1998, data are available for Lakes and Peninsula Borough (FIPS code 02164) for 1994-1998. Prior to 1994, death"
"counts and population estimates for this borough are aggregated with those for Dillingham Census Area (FIPS code 02070)."
"6. For CMF 1979-1998, data are available for Skagway-Yakutat-Angoon Census Area, Alaska (FIPS code 02231) only for 1989-93"
"Beginning with 1994, death counts and population estimates for this area are divided between Skagway-Hoonah-Angoon Census Area"
"(FIPS code 02132) and Yakutat Borough (FIPS code 02282)."
"7. For the years 1988 through 1991, if there were three or fewer deaths for a given Georgia county of residence (of deaths"
"occurring in Georgia) with HIV infection (ICD codes *042-*044, 795.8) cited as a cause-of-death (underlying or non-underlying"
"cause), these records were assigned a 'missing' place of residence code, Unknown County (code 13999). These deaths do not appear"
"in county death rates, but these deaths are included in the state and national death rates. More information:"
"http://wonder.cdc.gov/wonder/help/cmf.html#Unknown, Georgia."
"8. Beginning in 1989, deaths and population estimates for the Montana portion of Yellowstone Park (former county equivalent FIPS"
"code 30113) are included in Gallatin, MT (FIPS code 30031 ) and Park, MT (FIPS code 30067). More information:"
"http://wonder.cdc.gov/wonder/help/cmf.html#Yellowstone Park, Montana."
"9. For CMF 1979-1998, data are available for South Boston city, Virginia (FIPS code 51780) only for 1979-88. Beginning in 1989,"
"death counts and population estimates for South Boston city are reported with those for Halifax county (FIPS code 51083)."
"10. Deaths and population estimates are reported separately for Baltimore City (FIPS code 24510) and county (FIPS code 24005)."
"11. Deaths and population estimates are shown separately from the adjacent counties for Carson City, Nevada (FIPS code 32510)."
"12. Deaths for the city of Columbus, GA (previous FIPS code 13510) have been aggregated with Muscogee county, GA (FIPS code"
"13215)."
"13. Deaths and population estimates are reported separately for St. Louis City (FIPS code 29510) and county (FIPS code 29189)."
"14. Data are Suppressed when the data meet the criteria for confidentiality constraints. More information:"
"http://wonder.cdc.gov/wonder/help/cmf.html#Assurance of Confidentiality."
"15. Death rates are flagged as Unreliable when the rate is calculated with a numerator of 20 or less. More information:"
"http://wonder.cdc.gov/wonder/help/cmf.html#Unreliable."
"16. The population figures used in the calculation of death rates for the age group 'under 1 year' are the live births for the"
"given time period. More information: http://wonder.cdc.gov/wonder/help/cmf.html#Age Group."
"17. Population figures in this table for 1979 and 1981-89 are intercensal estimates of the July 1 resident population of the"
"United States. Note that the state and county population estimates for these years are not consistent with national estimates."
"The population figures in this table for 1980 and 1990 are modified age-race-sex (MARS) April 1 census counts. The population"
"figures for 1991-98 are bridged-race intercensal estimates of the July 1 resident population."